    "reviewed_associations": [
      "The seven blessing entry pages agree on name, I–IV values, actual melee variant, two bindings, and the shared effect summary.",
      "The blessing map, global/melee listings, source indexes, and both force-sword reverse rows point to the same two marks and summary.",
      "Canonical config and extension draft agree on the full trait ID, marks, RAW keys/hashes, icon attachment/path, and real newline-separated variant notes. Frozen agent trio and root own-tier/UI/RAW/image/routing/deferred-update evidence remain at the scoped hashes."
    ],
    "reviewed_deltas": [
      "Own I–IV values .02/.03/.04/.05 replace the wrapper fallback .01; formatter presents +2/+3/+4/+5%, and the exact full trait ID is bound to forcesword_2h_p1_m1 and _m2.",
      "The predicate is an eligible melee on_hit with current target_number >= 3, where ActionSweep supplies a current sweep ordinal. It is not a cumulative three-hit or three-positive-damage counter; event dispatch gates still apply.",
      "Proc storage is one boolean flag per event-processing batch. The buff extension updates buffs before proc events, so a successful event is consumed on the next Buff.update; multiple same-batch events coalesce, and no extra cooldown, stack, or timer is added.",
      "The held-slot condition is checked when the event is processed. A pending flag already set survives switching out before the next update; switching before the event check prevents creation.",
      "The consumer subtracts the tier fraction from current normalized peril and clamps to [0,1], returning to idle. IV gives 70%→65% (5 percentage points, 7.14% relative reduction), same-batch later ordinals still yield one decrement, a later batch can yield 65%→60%, and 3% clamps to 0%.",
      "Ordinary and powered melee ActionSweep hits can qualify; push itself is excluded while a follow-up sweep may qualify. For both marks, the separate Wind Slash extra attack is dispatched as ranged without target_number, and fling uses ActionDamageTarget ranged without target_number. Special toggle events themselves are not the blessing on_hit; the documented Wind Slash path is separately classified.",
      "RAW EN/ZH name and description keys and hashes match. All four static tier reconstructions preserve the source sentences with formatter values; errata is empty because the RAW wording is broader than the implementation rather than contradictory.",
      "The exploding-state consumer has an ability-interruption branch; the player text does not promise survival. UI names use the family/pattern/mark metadata for Mk VI and Mk VIII, and the verified image attachment is consistently referenced."
    ],
